            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A multi-element fiber scanner for scanning electromagnetic imaging radiation, the multi-element fiber scanner comprising: a base (110) having a base plane (107) and a longitudinal axis (112) orthogonal to the base plane (107); a first fiber link (940) passing through the base (110) in a direction parallel to the longitudinal axis (112), wherein the first fiber link is operatively coupled to at least one electromagnetic radiation source; a plurality of actuation elements joined to the base and extending from the base along the longitudinal axis; and a retention collar (130) disposed a predetermined distance along the longitudinal axis (112) from the base (110), wherein the first fiber link and the plurality of actuation elements are joined to the retention collar; a first set of piezoelectric tubes (905), wherein: a first piezoelectric tube (910) of the first set is joined to the base (110) and extends from the base (110); and a second piezoelectric tube (912) of the first set is joined to the retention collar (130) and extends from the retention collar (130); and a second set of piezoelectric tubes (905), wherein: a first piezoelectric tube (910) of the second set is joined to the base (110) and extends from the base (110); and a second piezoelectric tube (912) of the second set is joined to the retention collar (130) and extends from the retention collar (130).</p>
            </abstract>
